# Percentage scaling of decimal values

Verifies a decimal rate scales a decimal amount by hundredths in both operand orders. Multiplying 12.50 by 50% exercises the percentage rule that divides the percentage operand by 100 while keeping a plain decimal result.

>>> source
price: decimal = 12.50
half: decimal = 50%
print(price * half)
print(half * price)

<<< stdout
6.2500
6.2500

<<< stderr
